 "teaches": [
  "\"fit\": [places] frames them at the largest scale that fits the box both ways, centred, with the geography around them filling the rest: [\"Dubai\", \"London\", \"Singapore\"]; countries, cities, [lon, lat] and [from, to] pairs all fit",
  "\"fill\": true takes the height left in the column (a vertical weight), so the map follows the window; text scales with the map (0.8x to 1.5x labelSize) and labels that would collide on a small screen are hidden, cities before legs",
  "\"legs\": [{\"from\", \"to\", \"label\"}] draws several great-circle arcs, each label on its arc with a halo; \"legDistance\": true labels the unlabelled ones with their distance in km",
  "Labels are placed together when the document is built so they miss each other, the leg ends and the city names: no coordinates by hand"
 ],
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {},
  "clock": null,
  "touch": false
 },
 "check": {
  "describe": "Africa, Europe and South Asia around the six cities, the map filling the space under the header at every size (landscape shows more geography to the sides, not bands); five blue arcs from Dubai, each with its distance on a halo (London 5,473 km, Cairo 2,423 km, Delhi 2,205 km, Singapore 5,843 km, Johannesburg 6,419 km); text larger on large windows, no label on another label or on a city name.",
